{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489620-storypath-ultra-in-scion","id":1489620,"title":"Storypath Ultra in Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-10T03:17:21-07:00","id":1489620,"title":"Storypath Ultra in Scion","content":"Storypath Ultra is a new, standardized and improved version of the Storypath engine that will be implemented in new OPP studio products. It is supposed to unify the rules and make them easy to learn for new players. \ud83d\ude0e More info in the discussion below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/u52K_kfQYOk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/u52K_kfQYOk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/u52K_kfQYOk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/u52K_kfQYOk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T06:51:46-07:00","id":1489631,"title":"","content":"Major changes in Terminology <br /> Was Scale ( X Number) =&gt; Now Advantage ( X Number)<br /> Was 'You need X Successes to spend...' =&gt; Now 'You need X Hits to spend...'<br /> Stunts becomes Tricks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-10-2022, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:32:20-07:00","id":1490454,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm not really sure <i>why</i> the changes in terminology are needed, and I haven't watched the hour-long video, although I do think Storypath <i>should</i> be more unified - Scion and Trinity (for the two I know well) using different versions of Scale comes to mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:59:24-07:00","id":1490457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489620-storypath-ultra-in-scion?p=1490454#post1490454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm not really sure <i>why</i> the changes in terminology are needed, and I haven't watched the hour-long video, although I do think Storypath <i>should</i> be more unified - Scion and Trinity (for the two I know well) using different versions of Scale comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I didn't listen to the entire thing yet, but I do remember the reasoning for the change from &quot;Successes&quot; to &quot;Hits.&quot; As they phrased it, it was awkward to have something called a success--or multiple successes--on your dice, and yet not actually <i>succeed</i>.<br /> <br /> I remember less of why scale and stunts changed, but IIRC, part of scale was because and figuring it out as a comparative value is important.<br /> <br /> Also, worth noting: They won't be changing over Scion, at least within the current edition. They'll probably have a translation guide, but for now it'll run on the engine it's got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T21:06:06-07:00","id":1490483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489620-storypath-ultra-in-scion?p=1490454#post1490454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm not really sure <i>why</i> the changes in terminology are needed, and I haven't watched the hour-long video, although I do think Storypath <i>should</i> be more unified - Scion and Trinity (for the two I know well) using different versions of Scale comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did watch the video!<br /> <br /> The terminology changes basically have two reasons. In cases where they changed the underlying mechanics they also changed the terminology to make it clear to people that &quot;This works different now&quot; and then in some cases they changed terminology to help with clarity or remove awkward wording, like Mockery mentioned for rolled successes becoming hits.<br /> <br /> This is what I remember from watching the video last week...<ul><li>Ultra is basically written, but will be playtested with the new fantasy game line they have coming out (I forget the name).</li> <li>They don't plan on converting all of the existing Storypath games to use Ultra, but for game lines that are more contained they will probably start publishing new books using the Ultra rules (the easy example is They Came From... where each book contains the full rules, new They Came From... titles might use the Ultra rules since it would be easy to start using those moving forward. Scion and TC, not so much.)</li> <li>They are thinking about doing a translation guide, but it is very much in the &quot;We're thinking about it, but no concrete plans yet&quot; stage. The current idea is that the guide would be more guidance on how and when to use the Ultra rules, and not a &quot;This Boon now does X&quot; type of thing.</li> <li>They hope that basically 90+% of existing material in game lines they don't convert would still be usable if people decide to use the Ultra rules for their home table.</li> </ul>-----<ul><li>There was some talk about tweaking Difficulty and what it means, with a bigger emphasis on only rolling when dramatically important. If nothing interesting happens if someone fails the roll, then why are you bothering with a roll was the sort of general vibe.</li> <li>More hazy on this front, but I think they talked about wanting to make it easier and more clear on using Complications and have those on most rolls. Similar to Difficulty, if the roll isn't interesting enough to have a Complication, why are you bothering to roll?</li> <li>The overall vibe was they want to make sure the systems to apply mechanical stakes to rolls are clear and easy for Storyguides to use to make things fun and dramatic</li> </ul>-----<ul><li>Scale is renamed Advantage, which works similar but is meant to be much clearer about when it applies and how you get it. It sounds like they want to get back to the original conception of Scale, which is a very relative and situational thing but make it very clear when and how you get Advantage. Part of the name change was that the name Scale (and the examples given) are all sort of immutable things, Advantage sounds like something more situational and closer to how they want people to think about it.</li> <li>Advantage sounded like mechanically it mostly works like Scale does today though. It has a rating, you gain enhancement if you have Advantage based on the rating, if the other side has Advantage your Difficulty is higher. I forget if the &quot;if one side has 3 or more they win&quot; remains, but I think so.</li> <li>In general it sounded like they've been listening to the feedback on how Scale was presented in Origin and TC: Core, how is has been written and used in subsequent books, and want to make a fresh and clearer attempt at the original concept, without tossing out the parts that work well.</li> </ul>-----<ul><li>Skill Tricks from TC aren't in Ultra. The thought was that Gifts (powers some TC character types get) and Stunts covered a lot of the same conceptual ground as Skill Tricks so they existed in a kind of awkward space.</li> <li>Stunts are now Tricks, which sounds like there will be more options with what you can do with Hits than just Enhance or Complicate. I forget if this was explicit, but some of the ideas from Skill Tricks sounded like they'd become Trick options.</li> </ul>-----<ul><li>Paths will be a bigger deal, especially during character creation. It sounds like a lot more will be based on your Path choices, and the goal is for character creation to go a bit faster and cleaner and be fun to do. There are still Origin, Role, and Society Paths.</li> <li>Paths having ratings like they do in TC will be part of Ultra</li> <li>The vibe was that the mechanics for Paths will be revised a bit, but not dramatically so. That might be me reading into things though, I don't remember if they were explicit about mechanical changes to Paths outside of the two points above.</li> </ul>------<ul><li>Momentum will add Enhancement instead of dice, and there is an option to spend 2 momentum to turn a failure into a basic success (with no added enhancement from any source). Basically you can not fail, but you can't do anything extra and have to deal with any Complications.</li> </ul><br /> That is most of what I remember. Overall it sounded like the goal was to tighten up the base rules and apply lessons learned from the past five years. The lead on Ultra has written for Storypath a lot, and it felt like she has a very solid understanding about what works great and what could do with some clarification and improvement.<br /> <br /> It sounded like if you wanted to use some of the Ultra rules in Scion it wouldn't be that hard to do, and you could probably take a piecemeal approach without too much trouble. Mostly it sounded like a lot of clarification and refinement of the rules, not too many dramatic changes that would be hard to use with existing powers and things.<br /> <br /> Anyone else who listened please correct anything I got wrong or forgot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}